<description>
Replace the missing-marker cells so the whole grid has matching horizontal and vertical reflections.

Input structure:
- The grid is a complete reflection-symmetric pattern except for cells of one marker color.
- Under reflection across the horizontal and vertical center lines, each orbit has exactly one non-marker color.
- The marker color is structurally unique: treating any other color as missing breaks at least one orbit.

Rule:
- Group cells by their four-way reflection orbit: original, vertical mirror, horizontal mirror, and 180-degree mirror.
- Infer the unique marker color whose removal leaves one known color in every orbit.
- Fill every cell in each orbit with that known color.

Key insight:
- The yellow cells are not objects to move; they are holes in a two-axis mirror pattern, and their values are copied from the visible cells in the same reflection orbit.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "non-yellow pixels of a full-grid pattern with horizontal and vertical reflection symmetry",
  "transform": "group cells into four-way reflection orbits; infer yellow as the unique missing-cell marker, then fill each yellow pixel from the single visible color in its orbit"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16x16 (fixed, even dimensions)
  output_pattern:
    symmetry: full 4-way reflection (LR + UD, hence also 180-rot)
    colors: 7-8 colors from {1,2,3,5,6,7,8,9}; never uses 0 or 4
    structure: random colorful pattern in top-left 8x8 quadrant, reflected to fill grid
    each_orbit: 4 cells related by (r,c)->(r,W-1-c)->(H-1-r,c)->(H-1-r,W-1-c), all same color
  marker:
    color: 4 (yellow), always; never appears in the underlying symmetric pattern
    shape: exactly 2 disjoint axis-aligned rectangular blocks
    block_dims: 2-4 rows x 2-4 cols each; area 6-16 per block
    total_cells: 12-25 (sum of both blocks)
    placement: blocks in different quadrant-regions; never touch grid border [observed]
    solvability: every orbit containing a marker cell has >=1 non-marker cell
  input: output pattern with marker blocks replacing the underlying colors
  transform: for each marker cell, copy color from the non-marker cell in its 4-way orbit

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 7-8 colors from {1,2,3,5,6,7,8,9} (exclude 0 and 4).
    2. Fill the top-left 8x8 quadrant randomly using chosen colors.
    3. Reflect quadrant LR, UD, and diagonally to produce the full 16x16 symmetric output.
    4. Choose 2 random non-overlapping rectangles (2-4 rows x 2-4 cols each, total 12-25 cells).
       Place them avoiding row/col 0 and 15, in different quadrant-regions.
    5. Verify solvability -- no orbit has all 4 cells inside the marker rectangles.
       Reject and re-place if violated (low rejection rate since blocks are small).
    6. Replace marker-rectangle cells in the output with color 4 to produce the input.
```
</generation_spec>
